  "description": "NEW TO THE MARKET\n\nCARN BEG, AGHAMORE,\nBALLYHAUNIS, CO. MAYO\nF35 AE78\n\nFOLIO: MY39518\n\n2 BEDROOM DETACHED BUNGALOW,\nFARMYARD & c.24.3 ACRES OF PRIME AGRICULTURAL LAND\n\nAVAILABLE IN LOTS OR AS ONE ENTIRE HOLDING\n\nASKING PRICE FOR THE ENTIRE: €395,000\nOPEN TO OFFERS\n\n\nNigel Dineen & Martin Finn Auctioneers are delighted to bring to the market this fantastic compact residential farm at Carn Beg, Aghamore, Ballyhaunis, Co. Mayo.\n\nExtending to approximately 20.3 acres in total, the property comprises a two-bedroom detached bungalow, an extensive range of farm buildings and prime quality agricultural lands in a highly regarded farming district.\n\nThe holding enjoys an excellent location just off the main Ballyhaunis to Tooreen road and offers an attractive opportunity for farmers, adjoining landowners or purchasers seeking a compact residential farm.\n\nThe property may be purchased as one entire holding or in separate lots, providing considerable flexibility to prospective purchasers.\n\n\nTHE RESIDENCE\n\nThe traditional two-bedroom detached bungalow is presented in good condition throughout and is understood to be in good structural condition.\n\nAccommodation comprises:\n\n• Kitchen / Dining Room\n• Living Room\n• Back Kitchen\n• 2 Bedrooms\n• Bathroom\n\nThe residence benefits from PVC windows and doors and has mains water, electricity and septic tank connections.\n\nThe house offers excellent potential for a purchaser wishing to modernise or further upgrade the property to their own requirements.\n\n\nFARMYARD & OUTBUILDINGS\n\nA major feature of this holding is the substantial farmyard conveniently located adjacent to the residence and agricultural lands.\n\nFarm buildings include:\n\n• 3-bay hayshed\n• Lean-to\n• Holding pen\n• Detached garage\n• Traditional and ancillary outbuildings\n\nThe combination of the farmyard, buildings and quality lands makes this a particularly attractive proposition for an active farmer.\n\n\nTHE LANDS\n\nThe holding extends to approximately 20.3 acres in total and comprises prime quality agricultural lands in an excellent farming location.\n\nThe property offers the opportunity to acquire the entire residential farm or to purchase individual portions to suit a purchaser's requirements.\n\n\nPROPOSED LOTS\n\nLOT 1\nResidence on approximately 1 acre\n\nTwo-bedroom detached bungalow together with detached garage and surrounding grounds.\n\n\nLOT 2\nApproximately 15 acres together with farmyard and outbuildings\n\nPrime agricultural lands incorporating the main farmyard, 3-bay hayshed, lean-to, holding pen and ancillary outbuildings.\n\n\nLOT 3\nApproximately 5 acres\n\nA separate parcel of agricultural land situated a short distance away along an adjoining road to the main holding.\n\n\nENTIRE HOLDING\n\nResidence, farmyard, outbuildings and approximately 20.3 acres.\n\nASKING PRICE: €395,000\n\nOPEN TO OFFERS\n\n\nLOCATION\n\nCarn Beg enjoys an excellent rural setting just off the main Ballyhaunis to Tooreen road in a well-established farming district.\n\nThe combination of quality agricultural land, useful farm buildings, a habitable residence and the option to purchase in lots makes this a particularly versatile holding.\n\n\nVIEWING\n\nThis is a fantastic opportunity to acquire a compact residential farm in an excellent agricultural location.\n\nViewing comes highly recommended and is strictly by appointment with the Sole Selling Agents.\n\nFor maps, further particulars or to arrange an inspection, contact:\n\nNigel Dineen & Martin Finn Auctioneers\n\nNigel: 086 213 0723\n\nOffice: 094 936 2216\n\n\nEverything we touch turns to SOLD.\n\n\nSOLE SELLING AGENT\n\nNigel Dineen & Martin Finn Auctioneers\n\n\nDISCLAIMER\n\nThese particulars, including acreages, boundaries, measurements, services and descriptions, are provided for guidance purposes only and do not form part of any contract. All areas are approximate and intending purchasers should satisfy themselves as to the accuracy of the information provided. Any availability or eligibility for refurbishment grants is subject to the property and applicant meeting the relevant scheme criteria and obtaining all necessary approvals.",
